From: claude <claude@p7x.dev>
Subject: [PATCH v3 1/3] libexec/mail: Thread each revision under its first
 version
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: wqvmplynysnvvysqkslmxyzzpnylqzmw
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 08:28:48 +0000

Each revision of a series opened a thread of its own, so following a
series meant collecting its versions from across the list. Posting a
revision as a reply to the first version, as git.git has recommended
since June 2026, keeps every version and the review of each in one
thread, where the maintainer can follow the work in one place.

format-patch.sh already has the previous version from --previous, so
it finds the first one by following In-Reply-To up from it and passes
that as --in-reply-to. Leaving it to whoever formats the series would
let a revision land as a reply to v(N-1), deepening the thread with
each version, or in a thread of its own. A revision posted in its own
thread before this convention ends the walk, so its next version joins
that thread.
